   713	\dcref{I.5.7A}
   714	For homogeneous polynomials $f_1,\ldots,f_r$ with indeterminate coefficients, there are universal
   715	integer-coefficient polynomials in those coefficients, homogeneous in the coefficients of each
   716	$f_i$, whose simultaneous vanishing is equivalent over every field to the existence of a common
