    61	$\mathcal L(D)=\{f\in K(X):(f)+D\ge0\}\cup\{0\}$ and
    62	$l(D)=\dim_kH^0(X,\mathcal L(D))$.  The complete linear system is
    63	$|D|=\mathbf P H^0(X,\mathcal L(D))$; a linear system is base-point-free if
    64	no point belongs to every member, and very ample if it separates points and
    65	tangent vectors.  A divisor is ample precisely when it has positive degree.
    66	\end{definition}
    67	
    68	\begin{proposition}[Differential sequence]\label{ha-ch4-p21}\dcref{IV.2.1}
    69	\source{hartshorne-algebraic-geometry:IV.2.1}
